    "content" : "VI. NUMERICAL RESULTS"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 111,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 311.978, 163.014, 563.036, 270.66 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In this section, to get insight to the theoretical findings of the previous sections, we present a set of numerical results that compare the symbol error rates (SERs) of the quasiorthogonal and quasi-biorthogonal signaling methods against their respective orthogonal and biorthogonal counterparts. The goal here is to explore the amount of performance loss incurred as the non-orthogonality of the symbol vectors increases. Also, through numerical results, we examine the tightness of the upper bounds that were derived in Section V."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 112,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 311.978, 43.318, 563.041, 162.918 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
